<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n54951" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κατάπυκν-ος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
		strengthd. for <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πυκνός</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>thick, tufted</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἕρπυλλος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Theoc.
					<u>Ep.</u>
					1.1
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> Milit.,
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐν κ. στάσει</span> in <i>close</i>
			formation, <i><span class="en">
				Ascl.
				<u>Tact.</u>
				5.1
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> Medic.,
				<i>very costive</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κοιλίη</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hp.
				</span></i>
			<i>Acut.(Sp.</i>)<i><span class="en">
				56
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κ. εἰς σχηματισμόν</span>
			<i>often using</i> a formation, <i><span class="en">
				A.D.
				<u>Adv.</u>
				186.2
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡ διάλεκτος κ. ἐπὶ τὴν Χρῆσιν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Synt.</u>
					50.18
				</span></i>
			.</div>
